WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.909 --> 00:00:04.990
More often than not, beloved sitcoms finish
out with a finale that fits into one of a

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:05.900
few established archetypes.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:10.599
For example: the "will they or won't they
couple" finally gets together; one or more

00:00:10.599 --> 00:00:15.320
of the main characters move away; somebody
gets married; somebody has a baby; et cetera.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:19.840
In other words, major life events wrap up
the show with an eye to the future and tears

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:20.600
in the viewers' eyes.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.520
But not all big sitcom finales end in such
an emotional, chapter-closing fashion.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:30.230
TV history boasts some exceptions to the rule,
shows that bravely and boldly went against

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.300
the norm by going dark.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:36.220
Here are some of the most surprisingly twisted
final TV comedy episodes of all time.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.040
Seinfeld

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.980
Seinfeld was never a sticky-sweet, feel-good
sitcom.

00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:46.540
And in the hotly anticipated series finale,
all the selfish and thoughtless deeds committed

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:51.280
by Jerry, George, Elaine, and Kramer over
the years finally caught up with them.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:56.820
The gang nearly endures a plane crash, only
for the jet to land safely in a small Massachusetts

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.320
town.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:02.280
While there, they witness a crime firsthand
and make jokes about the victim while it's

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:02.780
happening.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.720
"See, the great thing about robbing a fat
guy is it's an easy getaway, ya know.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.540
They can't really chase you."

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:14.440
The victim mentions this while filing his
report with police, who arrest the Seinfeld

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.860
four for violating a "Good Samaritan" law.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:22.040
A slew of guest stars file through as character
witnesses at the ensuing trial, confirming

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:26.450
that the gang that audiences loved tuning
in to see every week all those years were

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:27.340
bad people.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:32.340
The show ends with the central four locked
up in prison, having learned nothing at all.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.060
How I Met Your Mother

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:39.640
To be fair, this CBS sitcom was titled How
I Met Your Mother and not "How I Spent Many

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:40.580
Years With Your Mother."

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.120
While it seemed like every woman Ted Mosby
dated over the years could've turned out to

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:50.220
be his kids' mother, the only real contender
seemed to be close friend and off-and-on girlfriend

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:50.720
Robin.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.560
The ninth and final season of the show switched
things up considerably.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:59.640
The entire run of episodes, except for the
finale, takes place over the weekend leading

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.220
up to Robin's wedding to Barney.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.780
Viewers finally find out that Ted lived happily
ever after with "The Mother," Tracy, until

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.880
she died of an illness in 2024.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:14.800
The series finishes up with middle-aged Ted
rekindling his romance with Robin, who divorced

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.640
Barney after three years of marriage.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:17.860
Death and divorce.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:18.760
What fun!

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:20.740
Dinosaurs

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.900
Dinosaurs ran on ABC from 1991 to 1994.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:30.000
It combined puppets and animatronics to create
a satirical series centered around the Sinclairs,

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:34.980
a middle-class family of dinosaurs living
in a prehistoric Pangea that bore a striking

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.100
cultural resemblance to '90s America.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:43.160
This cute and amusing family comedy ambitiously
concluded with a mass extinction event that

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:46.960
not only signaled the end for the Sinclairs,
but for all dinosaurs.

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:52.280
In an attempt to keep an invasive plant species
under control, a task force of dinosaurs spray

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:55.660
the planet with toxic chemicals, which wipes
out all plant life.

00:02:55.930 --> 00:03:00.400
The task force's idea to make plants grow
again by dropping bombs into volcanoes to

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:05.300
create rain clouds works too well, triggering
snow and a subsequent Ice Age.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:09.560
The episode ends with the Sinclairs holed
up in their house trying to stay warm and

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.660
stave off their imminent deaths.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:18.200
"And taking a look at the long-range forecast,
continued snow, darkness, and extreme cold."

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:20.380
ALF

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.760
NBC's ALF was a weird show about a sassy alien.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:28.680
He crash-landed in a suburban garage, loved
to eat cats, lazed around the house all day

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:33.270
watching TV and eating junk food, and told
tales about his bizarre life on his home planet

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:33.760
of Melmac.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.840
There were really only two ways that ALF could
end.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:42.040
In one scenario, ALF's identity is exposed
and he becomes an international celebrity.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:46.740
Or his identity is exposed and the government
comes to collect him and take him away to

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.560
a secret, scary research facility.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:53.340
As this was a family sitcom, one would think
option 1 would be the way to go.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:58.580
But nope, it ended with ALF whisked away to
an undisclosed location, where he presumably

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:00.860
endured all manner of pain and torture.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.460
"Just my luck… not a sports fan among you."

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:11.480
Patient fans had to wait until 1996's Project
ALF TV movie to learn he survived.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:13.160
M*A*S*H

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:19.850
The Korean War-set comedy/drama M*A*S*H finished
its 11-year run in 1983 with an extra-long

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:22.700
episode titled "Goodnight, Farewell, and Amen."

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:28.840
More than 106 million people tuned in, making
it the most-watched scripted program in American

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:29.620
TV history.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.620
There are a lot of laughs, a lot of tears,
and more of the gut punches about the many

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:38.520
horrors of war that the show famously wove
into the comedy over the years.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:43.940
While peace negotiations are underway, Hawkeye
Pierce sits in a therapy session, remembering

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:48.440
being on a bus with a Korean refugee woman
carrying an annoying chicken that wouldn't

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:49.300
stop squawking.

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:54.440
Hawkeye angrily ordered the fearful woman
to shut up the bird, which she did by snapping

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:54.940
its neck.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.300
With the help of his therapist, he uncovers
a repressed memory — it wasn't a bird, it

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.980
was the woman's baby, and she smothered it
out of fear.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:06.120
"It was a baby!

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:10.380
She smothered her own baby!"

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:14.580
That's about the darkest place a sitcom could
or would ever go.

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:16.860
The Mary Tyler Moore Show

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.520
The Mary Tyler Moore Show was revolutionary.

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:24.260
It was one of the first shows about an unmarried
woman, living on her own in a large American

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:27.260
city, focused on her career and friends rather
than romance.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:31.800
While it may have started as a vehicle for
its title star, it quickly became an ensemble

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.280
show because of all the great characters surrounding
her.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:39.430
There was grumpy news producer Lou Grant,
whip-smart news writer Murray Slaughter, and

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:43.340
news anchor Ted Baxter, the dumbest and most
arrogant man on television.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:47.920
After seven seasons, The Mary Tyler Moore
Show ended in 1977.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:53.340
The plot: A new station manager of WJM-TV
wants to boost the station's news ratings

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:58.580
and fires pretty much everybody… except
for Ted Baxter, the most incompetent employee.

